# Testing

`pytest` + `pytest-cov`. Tests live under `tests/`. Do not put tests inside `src/`.

## Layout

```
tests/conftest.py
tests/fixtures/          # tiny PNG/MP4 + masks (checked in, few KB)
tests/unit/              # engines, masks, io, selector — no ffmpeg if avoidable
tests/integration/       # short ~5s clip, CLI, Gradio optional smoke
```

Name files `test_<module>.py`, cases `test_<behavior>`.

## Unit — engines

- Each `InpaintEngine`: fixed fixture image + mask → compare to committed baseline with **SSIM ≥ threshold** and **PSNR ≥ threshold** (store thresholds in the test, not magic in production code).
- Pin seeds. Mark GPU tests `@pytest.mark.gpu` and skip without CUDA.
- Mock LaMa weights with a tiny stub tensor/ONNX in unit tests; real weights only in optional `@pytest.mark.slow`.

```python
# ✅ compare structure, not exact bytes if codec noise exists
assert ssim(out, baseline) >= 0.95
```

## Unit — auto-detect

- Fixture set: watermark at varied position/scale. Assert precision/recall of **candidates vs ground-truth mask** (IoU ≥ configured min).
- Never assert that a candidate is auto-applied.

## Integration — video

- Clip ~5s in `tests/fixtures/`. Assert: audio stream present, fps equals input (±epsilon), exit 0, no crash when the mask moves (keyframe fixture).
- Fake ffmpeg only in unit tests; integration must call real ffmpeg if present, else `@pytest.mark.skipif(not has_ffmpeg)`.

## Edge cases (required)

| Case | Expect |
|------|--------|
| Empty mask | `MaskError` unless allow flag |
| Full-image mask | `MaskError` or documented engine behavior + test |
| Tiny / huge resolution | reject or tile; no crash |
| Oversize file | `InputValidationError` before heavy decode |
| Missing LaMa weights | `EngineError`, no network |
| Output path == input | refuse without `--overwrite` |

## Mocking

- Mock network (`respx`/`unittest.mock`) — any test that would open a socket must fail.
- Do not mock `InpaintEngine.process` in that engine’s own unit tests.
- Time/progress: inject a clock/callback; do not `sleep` in tests.

## Coverage & TDD

- New engine/provider: write the failing contract test first (`process` shape/dtype, `get_mask` 0/255).
- Target: ≥80% on `src/watermark_remover/{engines,masks,io}`; do not chase 100% on Gradio layout.
- CI runs `pytest -m "not slow and not gpu"` by default.

## Determinism

Assert byte-stable PNG outputs for OpenCV Telea on the fixture. If an encoder is non-deterministic, compare metrics, not hashes.
